skill: "partner-ecosystem-mapping"
sections[3]:
  - "# partner-ecosystem-mapping\n\nMap the partner landscape by category, score candidates on reach, overlap and effort, and produce a ranked target list with written rationale. Use when entering a new channel, when a partnership underperforms for two consecutive quarters, or before any outreach campaign so pursuit effort is spent on scored targets, not guesses.\n\nOwner: role-partnership-bd-manager (pod-growth, marketing). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - search_web\n  - web_fetch\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"existing partner register partner-register.toon; category axes definition ecosystem-taxonomy.toon; product positioning summary from the current PRD\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/growth/partner-map.toon with categories[], candidates[] scored reach|overlap|effort 1-5, target_list[] with rationale\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load the ecosystem taxonomy; if the category axes for this market are undefined, draft them first and confirm with ask_question before scoring anything.\n2. Inventory current partners from partner-register.toon so new candidates are never duplicates of live agreements.\n3. Search the web per category for candidate programs; fetch each candidate's partner page through web_fetch and record the source URL next to the candidate.\n4. Score each candidate 1-5 on reach (audience size in the target segment), overlap (product adjacency without direct competition) and effort (integration and enablement cost).\n5. Reject any candidate scoring 5 on overlap with a direct competitor; adjacency is the point, competition is a conflict.\n6. Rank the remaining candidates by weighted score; keep the weights visible in the artifact rather than hiding them in the ranking.\n7. Write a one-sentence pursuit rationale per target naming the specific joint motion (integration, co-marketing, distribution) - never a generic 'strategic fit'.\n8. Emit ask_question to confirm the top targets before any outreach is sent; the manager owns the final pick.\n9. Write partner-map.toon and register pursued targets in partner-register.toon with status exploring.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ntargets to outreach; signed pursuits route through co-marketing-term-sheet-builder.\n"
